{
  "version": 1,
  "courseId": 995016,
  "courseSlug": "vuejs-2-the-complete-guide",
  "courseTitle": "Vue - The Complete Guide (incl. Router & Composition API)",
  "sourceLanguage": "en",
  "targetLanguage": "zh-TW",
  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "21879456",
      "title": "Using the Transition Component",
      "lectureOrder": 198,
      "videoOrder": 173,
      "sourceHash": "52f105ab4b7abc8db2e5b5caccaad6c57ac103b4357fc90648290aba91965cfd",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 1.461,
          "end": 3.15,
          "en": "So back in code,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 3.15,
          "end": 5.06,
          "en": "we've got this wrapped paragraph",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 5.06,
          "end": 8.77,
          "en": "and I mentioned that Vue would add certain utility classes.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 8.77,
          "end": 9.86,
          "en": "Well, it does.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 9.86,
          "end": 13.84,
          "en": "So let's define styles for them in the CSS code.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 13.84,
          "end": 16.06,
          "en": "You could do this anywhere, I'll do it here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 16.06,
          "end": 20.83,
          "en": "And the default class names Vue will add are v-enter-from,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 22.55,
          "end": 27.55,
          "en": "v-enter-active and v-enter-to.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 32.42,
          "end": 36.23,
          "en": "Vue, by default, will add these three CSS classes",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 36.23,
          "end": 38.38,
          "en": "at different times as explained",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 38.38,
          "end": 41.5,
          "en": "when the element is first added to the DOM.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 41.5,
          "end": 43.31,
          "en": "So in this case, when the paragraph",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 43.31,
          "end": 45.853,
          "en": "is appearing on the DOM for the first time.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 46.79,
          "end": 49.54,
          "en": "Now we can define different class styles here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 49.54,
          "end": 51.6,
          "en": "We can define different properties.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 51.6,
          "end": 54.25,
          "en": "And we should include at least one transition",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 54.25,
          "end": 58.93,
          "en": "or animation so that Vue is able to read the duration time",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 58.93,
          "end": 61.26,
          "en": "from these classes because I mentioned",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 61.26,
          "end": 63.73,
          "en": "that this would be another key thing it does",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 63.73,
          "end": 64.913,
          "en": "behind the scenes.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 66.17,
          "end": 69.43,
          "en": "Now, in v-enter-from, you define your starting state.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 69.43,
          "end": 70.9,
          "en": "And for this paragraph,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 70.9,
          "end": 73.53,
          "en": "that could be that it initially is invisible",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 73.53,
          "end": 75.66,
          "en": "by setting opacity to zero.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 75.66,
          "end": 78.42,
          "en": "And maybe that it's moved up a little bit",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 78.42,
          "end": 83.42,
          "en": "by setting transform to translateY -30 pixels.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 85.03999999999999,
          "end": 89.43299999999999,
          "en": "This moves it up a little bit above its real position.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 90.97,
          "end": 93.88,
          "en": "In v-enter-to, we have the end state,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 93.88,
          "end": 96.39,
          "en": "so the final state we wanna have at the end.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 96.39,
          "end": 99.07,
          "en": "And there, we can have an opacity of one",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 99.07,
          "end": 102.50999999999999,
          "en": "and set transform: translateY to zero",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 102.50999999999999,
          "end": 103.99000000000001,
          "en": "to take the real position",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 103.99000000000001,
          "end": 106.60300000000001,
          "en": "of the element it should have on the page.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 108.03,
          "end": 111.2,
          "en": "And v-enter-active is now the place",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 111.2,
          "end": 112.6,
          "en": "where you, for example,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 112.6,
          "end": 115.32,
          "en": "add the transition CSS property",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 115.32,
          "end": 119.67,
          "en": "to tell Vue to watch for all CSS properties",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 119.67,
          "end": 121.2,
          "en": "that might be animated.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 121.2,
          "end": 123.53,
          "en": "So in this case, opacity and transform,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 123.53,
          "end": 126.39,
          "en": "which are the two properties changing here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 126.39,
          "end": 128.36,
          "en": "then you define a duration.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 128.36,
          "end": 130.423,
          "en": "That is what Vue will read.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 131.3,
          "end": 133.19,
          "en": "So what Vue will take to find out",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 133.19,
          "end": 136.67000000000002,
          "en": "how long these classes should be added to the element.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 136.67000000000002,
          "end": 138.823,
          "en": "And then your easing function.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 140.21,
          "end": 143.21,
          "en": "And if you do that, and you reload,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 143.21,
          "end": 145.06,
          "en": "you can click Toggle Paragraph",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 145.06,
          "end": 149.969,
          "en": "and you have this animation for adding the paragraph.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 149.969,
          "end": 151.873,
          "en": "For removing, we don't have any yet",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 151.873,
          "end": 153.70600000000002,
          "en": "but for adding, we do.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 154.87,
          "end": 157.07,
          "en": "Well, and I already showed it on the slide.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 157.07,
          "end": 159.903,
          "en": "You have similar classes for removing.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 160.75,
          "end": 165.57,
          "en": "There we have the v-leave-from class.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 165.57,
          "end": 169.32999999999998,
          "en": "We have the v-leave-active class",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 169.32999999999998,
          "end": 173.513,
          "en": "and we have the v-leave-to class.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 174.87,
          "end": 177.028,
          "en": "And it's the same concept as for entering.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 177.028,
          "end": 179.46,
          "en": "We define our starting state,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 179.46,
          "end": 181.36,
          "en": "which for me here is the same state",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 181.36,
          "end": 183.41,
          "en": "as the end state for entering",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 183.41,
          "end": 185.03,
          "en": "but it doesn't have to be the same.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 185.03,
          "end": 187.41,
          "en": "You can define a totally different state here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 187.41,
          "end": 190.33,
          "en": "totally different CSS properties as well.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 190.33,
          "end": 191.21,
          "en": "That is fine.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 191.21,
          "end": 194.74,
          "en": "You don't have to use the same CSS properties",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 194.74,
          "end": 195.653,
          "en": "as for adding.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 196.76,
          "end": 197.86,
          "en": "But here I'm doing it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 198.91,
          "end": 201.68,
          "en": "In v-leave-to, I use the same state",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 201.68,
          "end": 205.16,
          "en": "as I had for entering in my from state.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 205.16,
          "end": 207.51,
          "en": "Now it's the to state for leaving,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 207.51,
          "end": 210.193,
          "en": "making this invisible and moving it up a bit.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 212.2,
          "end": 214.14,
          "en": "Or actually, let's move it down a bit",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 214.14,
          "end": 216.51,
          "en": "by setting this to +30 pixels,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 216.51,
          "end": 218.85,
          "en": "also to emphasize that you don't have",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 218.85,
          "end": 221.127,
          "en": "to use the same styles as before.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 221.127,
          "end": 223.51,
          "en": "And for v-leave-active,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 223.51,
          "end": 225.9,
          "en": "I have the same transition set in here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 225.9,
          "end": 228.45,
          "en": "but instead of ease-out, I'll use ease-in",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 228.45,
          "end": 230.383,
          "en": "for a different easing function,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 231.53,
          "end": 234.19,
          "en": "which just controls how that duration",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 234.19,
          "end": 236.823,
          "en": "is split across the different steps.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 238.17000000000002,
          "end": 240.67,
          "en": "And now if you save that and reload,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 240.67,
          "end": 243.55,
          "en": "we have animation for entering",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 243.55,
          "end": 246.253,
          "en": "and also for removing like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 247.42,
          "end": 250.71,
          "en": "Now, that is how you can use the transition component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 250.71,
          "end": 253.86,
          "en": "to animate the appearance and removal",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 253.86,
          "end": 255.89,
          "en": "of HTML elements.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 255.89,
          "end": 259.01,
          "en": "And especially the removal is something",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 259.01,
          "end": 261.47,
          "en": "which was harder without transition.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 261.47,
          "end": 262.95,
          "en": "But also for entering,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 262.95,
          "end": 267.54,
          "en": "you gain more flexibility with that transition component,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 267.54,
          "end": 269.73,
          "en": "which you wrap around the element,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 269.73,
          "end": 271.89,
          "en": "which does use v-if or v-show",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 271.89,
          "end": 274.18,
          "en": "and which then should be animated.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 274.18,
          "end": 277.22,
          "en": "You don't need it if you're not having this v-if",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 277.22,
          "end": 278.73,
          "en": "or v-show case",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 278.73,
          "end": 281.01,
          "en": "because if you just have something like the block",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 281.01,
          "end": 282.35,
          "en": "in the first example,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 282.35,
          "end": 283.65999999999997,
          "en": "in the last lectures,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 283.65999999999997,
          "end": 286.88,
          "en": "you can just conditionally add and remove CSS classes",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 286.88,
          "end": 288.01,
          "en": "as you learned it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 288.01,
          "end": 290.59000000000003,
          "en": "It's just this added to the DOM",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "start": 290.59000000000003,
          "end": 292.85,
          "en": "or removed to the DOM case",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 103,
          "start": 292.85,
          "end": 295,
          "en": "where you can't do that",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 104,
          "start": 295,
          "end": 297.21,
          "en": "because the element is just not there",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 105,
          "start": 297.21,
          "end": 299.933,
          "en": "and that's where transition then helps you.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "errors": []
}
